  "description": "Write CUDA C/C++ kernels inline inside C# source files using raw string literals, annotate\n      a partial method with [GpuKernel], and let the KernelSharp MSBuild task compile them with\n      NVRTC (NVIDIA Runtime Compilation) — no subprocess, no Visual Studio required. The compiled\n      PTX is embedded directly in your assembly. Supports build-time and runtime compilation modes,\n      strongly-typed CudaBuffer<T> device pointers, parallel multi-kernel compilation,\n      gzip-compressed PTX embedding, and zero-configuration GPU detection at runtime.",
